T: Domestic Violence
C: International
D: 2026
O: Prof. Don Dutton
B: A study by Prof. Don Dutton of 6,321 partner homicides found domestic violence often did not precede intimate partner homicide. Only 6.5% of female victims had experienced domestic violence in the preceding month, and 5% of heterosexual male victims were perpetrators of violence in the month preceding the homicide, indicating women mostly do not kill male partners in self-defence.
U: https://connect.springerpub.com/content/sgrpa/early/2026/02/14/pa-2025-0046
