H: Studies Link Male Perpetrated Intimate Partner Homicide to Suicide Attempts
T: Domestic Violence
C: USA
D: NA
O: Velopulos et al./Dutton and Kerry/Eliason
B: A list of studies shows most male perpetrators of intimate partner homicide also attempt suicide, suggesting acknowledging male pain could indirectly help reduce female suffering. The US NVDRS found 46.5% of male perpetrators also attempted suicide (Velopulos et al., 2019). One in three had attempted suicide post-homicide (Dutton and Kerry, 1999). Perpetrators of murder-suicide had profiles consistent with suicidal people, not murderers, with a history of suicide attempts but not aggression (Eliason, 2009).
U: NA
