H: Lesbian Women Show Higher Partner Abuse Victimization Rates Than Heterosexual Women
T: Domestic Violence
C: USA
D: 2016/17
O: CDC
B: It has been a established fact that lesbian women are more likely to be victims of partner abuse (x22%) than heterosexual women. Many try to argue that since lesbian relationships involve two women that explains their high rate of victimization. But the study concerned does not measure combined rates of both parties, rather it measures individuals. The original claim is also based on violence within intimate relationships, not general experience of violence. Some people also claim that the high rates maybe due to lesbians being in relationship with violent men, which is an assumption as the study doesn't measure that either. This argument is further debunked by the fact that gay men have far lesser rates of violence than lesbians, which would otherwise imply, lesbians date men more than gay men, which is illogical.
U: https://www.cdc.gov/nisvs/documentation/nisvsReportonSexualIdentity.pdf
