T: Domestic Violence
C: UK
D: 2025
O: Office for National Statistics
B: An ONS survey published in November 2025 estimated 1.5 million men and 2.2 million women were victims of domestic abuse in England and Wales in the previous year. Of these, 425,000 (51%) men and 409,000 women were victims of current partner abuse. Breakdown by abuse type (percentage of men:women) included: emotional abuse 55:45; economic abuse 56:42; health abuse 75:25; threats 56:44; physical abuse 50:50; sexual assault 14:86; stalking 33:67. Prior to this release, methodological changes led to a 42% increase in recorded female victims and a 111% increase in recorded male victims compared to previous data.
