H: PASK Project: Large-Scale Review Finds Near Gender Symmetry in Partner Abuse
T: Domestic Violence
C: blank
D: blank
O: Partner Abuse State of Knowledge (PASK)
B: The Partner Abuse State of Knowledge (PASK) project, conducted by 42 scholars and 70 research assistants across 20 institutions over two years, reviewed 12,000 studies and summarised 1,700 in tables, finding near gender symmetry. Lifetime prevalence of partner abuse was 23% for women and 19.3% for men; perpetration rates were 28.3% for women and 21.6% for men. Of total violence, 57.9% was bidirectional, 28.3% unidirectional female-to-male, and 13.8% unidirectional male-to-female. Motives behind violence were found similar across genders: anger, jealousy, emotional hurt, difficulty expressing verbally, and seeking partner's attention.
U: https://domesticviolenceresearch.org/
