H: Young people who experience bullying are more likely to fantasise about committing acts of violence
T: Violence due to bullying
C: Switzerland
D: 2021
O: University of Cambridge
B: A study tracking 1,465 young people in Zurich at ages 15, 17 and 20 found that experiencing multiple forms of bullying was closely associated with violent fantasies. Among 17-year-old boys with no victimisation, the probability of violent fantasies was 56%, rising to 97% for those reporting ten types of mistreatment. For girls, it rose from 23% to 73%. About 25% of 17-year-old boys reported a fantasy of killing someone they knew in the past 30 days.
U: https://www.cam.ac.uk/research/news/young-people-who-experience-bullying-are-more-likely-to-fantasise-about-committing-acts-of-violence
